<title>AUSTRALIA: Qantas plans interactive entertainment.</title>
<headline>Qantas plans interactive entertainment.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1997-07-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Australia's Qantas Airways Ltd was proceeding with plans to install interactive entertainment systems in its international fleet, a company spokesman said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Qantas was reviewing a number of suppliers and was hopeful of reaching decision in the next four months, he added.</p>
<p>He had been asked to comment on a statement made in Phoenix, Arizona, by Interactive Flight Technologies Inc on Tuesday that Qantas had decided not to install a new interactive in-flight entertainment system for its long haul fleet.</p>
<p>-- Sydney newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
</text>
